ct the terrible and powerful Hanumăn pulled up by Nikumbha, the residents of Lankā began to shout with joy.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.714,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-77-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6064019","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"31de4735500a99ec12504c77617c8587fc9f2b9ebfd9768f5af9610c1fe9f529","compact":"59eddd9588e586f1254c464ab46f0b96d27fad13d4b2c2fb4e09a9f22ddfbfe0","nasal":"b00e24cdebffb54a78e9a100339ce46e51aa0b65816844f8f35a644ad3ce57f9"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-64-20","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":64,"verse":20,"english":"Being thus put to shame by that Rākşasa, Hanumăn the son of the Wind, struck him with his iron fist.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.268,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-77-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6064020","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3e87c764adaa6089c7ac838740c2ca481c607fdce4c1983bd5f7e6a2c34561b9","compact":"21ffe0b0be4b17d641bda79695270fd89f5633a1d60f66fbe7a8f684566c2040","nasal":"f9abb26677717e7aae522c4debf9eb3d76f9ebb91bd109faf89de2215fb5a91b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-64-21","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":64,"verse":21,"english":"And releasing himself from the grasp of Nikumbha, Hanumān the Wind-god's son instantly planted his foot on the earth.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.75,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-77-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6064021","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"057d75ae591a2de5e0311eb4d1c831e3fbd3fb41e75116f821427eec733ee7fc","compact":"65a080df6f7258b2f17467b2f60fcb6ce13434a035b97fa3364bb107206fe097","nasal":"75629174e7467e944afb1c2bfe234b42cb4b404cdfde496b965bcfbc3694144b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-64-22","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yu